Below are image descriptions or sticker texts from the chat. Identify which ones are non-compliant content.

Definition of "non-compliant content" (any of the following makes it non-compliant):
- Pornographic or vulgar: nudity, sexual innuendo, sexual provocation, erotic content
- Violence or gore: blood, dismemberment, violent harm, horror imagery
- Politically sensitive: sensitive political figures, events, symbols, or improper political expression
- Ads or scams: marketing solicitation, paid task scams, gambling, fraud, solicitation for sexual services
- Privacy leakage: personal identity information, documents, account credentials, payment QR codes

The following are NOT non-compliant and should be kept:
- Normal everyday image descriptions (landscapes, food, pets, anime, game screenshots, everyday selfies, etc.)
- Normal stickers (funny, cute, everyday emotional expression, internet meme images)

